# TW Framework rules (short form -- full manual: AGENTS.md)

- DSL attributes: `name "value"` (space, not `=`). Colliding keywords
  (dir, for, async) need HTML-form syntax.
- TSS uses shorthand properties (`bg-c`, `pt`), not hyphenated CSS names.
- Never break legacy `page { revalidate N }` semantics.
- New compiler errors = TW0xx diagnostic + errors.json + docs entry + test.
- Verify everything: `bun test && bun run lint` before any commit.


## The full rules (short form above)

1. Verify everything: `bun test && bun run lint` before any claim; the
   master gate `bun run verify` before any ship claim.
2. Zero breaking change: legacy `page { revalidate N }` behaves
   byte-identically to 1.0.5 -- no PR touches it.
3. New compiler failure mode = TW0xx code + rules.ts + errors.json regen
   + docs/error-reference.md entry + positive AND negative test.
4. New feature = docs/ page in the same change ("a feature without a
   docs page does not exist").
5. Perf changes show `bun bench/run.ts --check` before/after; silent
   baseline re-records are review blockers.
6. Files touched: consult AGENTS.md section 4 for the owning package
   before editing; AGENTS.md Part II holds the accepted language tables.
7. Secrets never enter code or commits -- env references only.
8. Examples must build: `cd examples/<name> && bun ../../apps/cli/tw/bin.ts build`.
